WEBVTT

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:47.250
That's the place.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.870
I never expected...

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.830
...to come back here again.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.840
There's that old familiar smell.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.040
Hey, the door isn't over there--

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.980
Huh?

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.850
Already disposed of.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.970
Not even being able to
read minds would help with him.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:51.480
Qiongqi...

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.530
"A Certain Scientific Accelerator"

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.930
"#03 Numbers (Charms of the Four Perils)"

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.310
I never figured on you
being the one to come to me...

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:30.890
Huh?

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.460
...Esther.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.360
Hishigata...

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.240
...Mikihiko.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:46.620
But your timing is perfect.
Qiongqi has been completed.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.910
I wanted you to see it
more than anyone. Mm-hmm.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.870
Do you think you can just get away
with making something like this?!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.830
It's a little late to be asking that, Esther.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.800
You're the one who taught me
everything there is to know

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.240
about animating dead bodies, aren't you?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.050
You don't mean... Taotie
and Hundun are already...?

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.010
Yeah.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:11.310
I've incorporated the evil spirits of
the Numbers that your family created.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.520
I have nothing but gratitude for you. Mm-hmm.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:19.110
It took a lot of dead bodies for us
to make this many souls, huh?

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.530
You have to stop!

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.110
Have you gotten spooked?

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:25.280
You were manipulating the dead
at your whim, too, remember?

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.160
You're wrong! I was--

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.830
I'm not wrong.
From the view of the dead body,

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.120
they still end up being used
to serve the pleasure of the living.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.630
You're no different, Esther.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.060
Stop...

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:43.970
You have to stop.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:48.810
Hey! What the hell are
you rambling on about?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.400
Ah, so you're Accelerator,
are you? Mm-hmm...

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.600
You're Last Order's guardian?

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.240
Someday, I'd like to have you as a subject.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:06.860
Huh?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:11.360
Is using corpses to play dress-up dolls
becoming a thing these days?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.840
Not even I would go that far.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:21.170
Don't be so cold. In a sense,
I'm complimenting your killing.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.850
Ooh, momentum, heat,
and wow, even electricity?

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.140
Vector control can do
just about anything, huh?

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.140
I guess when you use your ability,

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.850
the amount of information
around you increases.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.650
I wonder if the key to your
ability lies in there somewhere.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.320
But either way, you're just a bystander here.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:49.060
Besides, there's nothing for me
to gain by fighting you just now.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:50.490
So...

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.230
I think I'll make a tactical retreat.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.420
There's no way I'm letting
you get out of here!

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:11.580
Tch.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.850
I have all sorts of data on you.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:15.930
Huh?

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:19.650
The object of your vector control
is whatever you touch.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:23.020
In the event you aren't in contact,
which is to say, at a distance,

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.530
your attacks are no different
than any other physical phenomenon.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.200
The versatility of this psychokinesis,
boosted to Level 5 class as it is,

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.370
is really something, isn't it?

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.080
Huh?

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.340
Did you say Level 5?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.340
Mm-hmm. Well,

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.010
I'll see you later.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:00.140
Tch.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.730
Hishigata is right.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:11.180
I've been doing the
same things that he's done.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.490
I've controlled the dead to do my bidding.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.540
I used them.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.040
So what?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:19.970
Huh?

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.180
I thought you were trying to stop him.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:46.250
"I went and bought three lunches,
just like you asked,"

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.440
proudly reports Misaka Misaka,

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:53.550
without saying anything about
the snack for herself she also bought.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:54.810
Hey!

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.330
That girl you're sitting
across the bed from--

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.800
who might she be?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.000
Who might you be?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.090
--That's--
--I wasn't asking you!

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:11.420
Well?

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.470
Who might you be?

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.720
--I'm Esther Rosenthal. I do necromancy--

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:21.710
--Hey!
--I'm Esther Rosenthal. I do necromancy--

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:30.530
I-I'm, um, something like
a classmate of Accelerator's.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.950
I'm here to ask him for some help.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:33.820
"Nice to meet you,"

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:39.160
says Misaka Misaka,
glancing over at your expression,

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.130
wondering what that
eye contact was all about.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:47.790
There's something you're
hiding from me, all right.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.220
You two-timer!

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.110
Hey...

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:09.900
Damn it. We're hungry. What the hell?

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.480
"Hmph. W-We could all
go to a restaurant, right?"

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:20.370
says Misaka Misaka, giving you the
chance to apologize for your infidelity.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:25.490
Tch, I'm getting tired of
the family restaurant, damn it.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.130
Y-You're not mad?

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.130
I make it a policy to avoid the pointless.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:33.590
Hooray!

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:36.220
"Hey, can I order what I want today?"
asks Misaka Misaka...

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:41.430
This is a human guinea pig who has
experienced death over 10,000 times?

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.040
She's unbelievable.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.230
Let's go.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:05.370
What is this? I don't recognize
a single dish on here!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.660
Oh, you don't say.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.130
What kind of food is this "bee f'curry"?

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:12.320
It's curry.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.510
Curry!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:18.590
What kind of meat does it contain?
Is it sheep? Is it goat?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.890
It's beef.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.600
Yes, cow meat.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.350
And these cheese-stuffed--

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.810
Hamburger.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:26.270
Also cow meat!

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.480
You know everything, don't you?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.810
Sure do! Ask me anything!

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.700
All right.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.730
What kind of food is this?

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.320
Crunchy food, bursting with yummy flavor!

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.490
Pork deep-fried in oil.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:41.820
And this?

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:46.540
Ah! It's a creamy, 
piping-hot, delicious food!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:51.540
Flavored rice with a
fried chicken egg stuck on top of it.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:52.580
And this?

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:56.550
A lumpy, tasty, delicious food!

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.840
Salmon eggs pickled in soy sauce
and served over rice.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.140
And this?

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:06.140
A hot, melt-in-your-mouth yummy food!

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.600
A stewed tuna head.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.980
"All of the food here is very delicious!"

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.280
says Misaka Misaka, letting you know.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.200
Everything is delicious,
and everyone is happy, huh?

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.180
Here is your order.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.670
This is very, very, <i>surprisingly</i> good--

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.420
This is very good, too.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.760
Good, isn't it?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:48.350
Good food tastes better when eaten together.
This is what families do.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.740
It is a tremendous feast.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:56.360
I've never had anything
as wonderful as this around me.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:01.860
The science of Academy City
is quite marvelous!

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:04.950
This has nothing to do with science.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.030
All right, my turn.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:08.830
Is that for me?

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.290
This is what families do.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.630
Mm, it's good!

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:20.840
Where are you going?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.380
Gotta make a call.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:27.500
Those phony Antiskill guys
called themselves "DA."

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.290
Whatever the case, they're up to no good.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.350
I need someone who's familiar
with folks up to no good.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:40.430
Someone who might know
something about DA would be...

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:47.990
What's up?

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:52.200
Quick question for you.
Yoshikawa, do you know who DA is?

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.420
DA?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:57.500
A dark side organization
who seems to have ties to Antiskill.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.080
From what I saw of their weapons,
they're pretty well off, too.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:07.520
Villains who love to play with dolls,
and have a real passion for justice.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.550
I don't know them.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.240
But, I can check into them.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:14.460
Thanks.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:19.000
You're being awfully amenable.
Does this have to do with that girl?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:34.220
You only ever get like this
when you're with her.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.000
Cram it. I'm hanging up.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.970
"We ate it all! Your friend goofed up at
the fountain and drenched us, so we went
back to my room! Take care of the bill!!"

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.150
Tch.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:12.950
Huh?

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:22.290
"Jeez! It's good manners to knock,
even for your own room!"

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:26.880
says Misaka Misaka, drilling into you
the obvious, which you can't seem to do!

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.840
Taking that kind of care is very important!

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:30.550
Oh, is that right?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.560
Wh-What's going on?
Why are you starting a fight?

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.560
"Why are you still not dressed?!"

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:41.730
says Misaka Misaka, agitated by
this woman's overly-bold appearance.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.520
What do you mean?

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:50.320
Oh, my clothes? They're in drying right now.
Besides, it doesn't bother me.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.260
"You have to let it bother you!"

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:56.290
says Misaka Misaka, unsure of what
the sense the person in front of her has,

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.770
and shuddering!

00:14:58.370 --> 00:14:59.290
Why?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.290
"They're called feminine sensibilities!"

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:06.510
says Misaka Misaka, showing off the
knowledge she acquired reading books.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:12.360
Is that right? Okay. I'll be more
careful from now on.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.930
It's pretty loud in here, huh?

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.440
Okay, Last Order, it's just
about time for your checkup.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:20.170
Mm-hmm.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.280
"Okay, I'll see you later," says Misaka Misaka
with a somewhat lonely face,

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.110
trying to get your attention.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.570
You can't have it.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:35.120
And have him fix what's wrong
with your head while he's at it.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.000
There's no need! Nyah!

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.260
--"Oh, the usual room, right?"
--Mm-hmm.

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:47.000
...says Misaka Misaka, running off
like the wind, leaving only her words!

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:56.600
Incidentally, about that girl, Hitokawa Hasami,
that Antiskill wanted me to take a look at...

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:00.790
There was nothing I could do for her.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:05.610
Not three days after her death.
It was out of my hands.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:06.810
Not interested.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:07.860
However,

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:12.570
I did find this inside her mouth.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.830
Well, I have a checkup to perform, so...

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.340
What is this?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.830
A low-level spiritual charm.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:24.380
Huh?

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.340
Do you have a few moments?

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.510
"Morgue"

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:38.100
My family created a kind of necromancy
whereby we can transplant a false soul

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.980
into a dead body, and freely control it.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.850
But what we have here isn't a dead body;

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.810
it's a person.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:52.280
I taught him how to do necromancy
without understanding that.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.440
I was warned against carelessly
teaching others how to do it.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:02.120
But because of me, she was used
to do something abominable.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.950
Let's have a little look, here.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.800
Sure enough, the conduit is still open.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.470
As it stands, she'd call down
her drifting residual information.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:24.230
Even if Hitokawa Hasami were buried
in a grave, she'd crawl back out of it.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:28.480
And not just that--if her
vessel is left neglected,

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.980
she'll be unable to pass
through Heaven's gates.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.240
I'm going to restart Hitokawa Hasami.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:40.200
I'll also reaffix a Huotou,
a false soul that I created,

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.700
and then close her spiritual conduit.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.870
Is this her ability?

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:47.530
She must be using history and
legend to reinforce her own paradigm,

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:51.340
and then extending out her Personal Reality.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.780
You'll be all right now.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.300
What...

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:01.600
...is that?

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.690
Stop!

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:08.060
Hasami?

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:10.920
Hasami!

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:14.820
Why do you do these kinds of things?

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.520
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.200
Hasami!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.310
I'm sorry!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.630
Hasami, what's wrong?

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:31.850
I'm sorry.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:36.050
Hasami, I got a call from
your school. What happened?

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:37.130
I'm sorry.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.470
What's going on?!

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:39.390
I'm sorry!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:43.310
What's the matter?
Has something happened, Hasami?

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:44.430
I'm sorry.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:48.100
What's the matter, Hasami?
Answer me! Hasami!

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.520
I'm sorry.

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:57.880
I'm... sorry...

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:07.510
H-Huh? I'm still alive...

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.080
She appears to have
regained consciousness.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:13.460
That explains it.
She's a Level 2 pyrokinesist.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:16.960
Not a half-bad subject.
Her ability is suited for combat.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.340
Best of all, she's an "evil" criminal
who's guilty of suicide.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:20.990
Huh?

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:24.210
Good. Let's go ahead and dispose of her.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:30.390
Rest easy. We will use your body
to serve the cause of justice.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:32.760
Stop!

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.360
Are you all right?

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:41.280
No problem.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:45.740
You startled me, touching her residual
thoughts without any warning like that.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:48.500
Uncontrolled residual thoughts
can be dangerous information,

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:52.040
and people sometimes refer
to them as site-bound spirits.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:57.380
We necromancers use these
residual thoughts as a key code,

00:19:57.380 --> 00:20:00.220
to let us slip a pseudo-soul into the body.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.220
Looks like I was successful.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:07.430
Now, once my Huotou is affixed to her,
I can close up her conduit.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:10.690
Give it just a moment.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:17.320
What was that tremendous amount of data?
A mind-reading ability?

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.970
One that specializes in the dead, at that.
Still, it was weird, considering.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.370
Moreover, that last vision I saw...

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:29.500
Those guys will go so far
as to kill to get bodies?

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:32.620
What are you two doing here?

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.170
This is no place for children to be playing.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.300
Get on out of here, now.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.310
Why, these...

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.470
Come on, out you go, now.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:47.270
Move it!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:49.810
Things have taken a bad turn.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:50.270
What?

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.600
My Huotou has already
become affixed to Hitokawa Hasami.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:58.610
She might start to move
in front of those men.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.400
That will be the least of
their worries in a second.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.860
Huh? Damn it, where is it?

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:06.660
What's wrong?

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.030
The solution...

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:11.000
Hey, without that,
we can't dispose of the corpse.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.000
Hey...

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.620
Are you still here? Get going--

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:16.790
By "solution," do you mean <i>this</i>?

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.250
How did you get your hands on that?!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:22.590
Heh, what were you planning to do with this?

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:28.100
Whatever. Once it's gone, it won't matter!

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:37.310
Way to dodge that.
But then, this is more like it.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.610
Damn it, he's making a mockery of us.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:45.160
Then again, disciplining naughty
children is a part of our job.

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:52.780
Now then...

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.120
It's time...

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.500
...to bring about some justice!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:37.000
"Next time"

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:41.530
"Third Number"
